# SwiftFormat runs on an explicit allowlist, not on its defaults.
#
# The default rule set restyles this repo rather than repairing it: it rewrites
# `case .pointsTo(let target, ...)` into `case let .pointsTo(target, ...)`, moves
# `public` from the member onto the extension, and breaks every hugging closing
# paren onto its own line — 55 of 61 files, none of it a defect. The rules below
# are the ones that fix real noise and leave the house style alone.

--swiftversion 6.0

--rules trailingSpace,consecutiveBlankLines,blankLinesAtEndOfScope,linebreakAtEndOfFile,redundantSelf,redundantReturn,redundantParens,duplicateImports,sortImports

--exclude **/.build,**/DerivedData
